internal resistance of the voltmeter is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F463a009e-db76-4f86-8f1b-698f0c0c9b2e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 260px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "8ebe44", "text": "<math><mn>35</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b746a"}, {"id": "c9d88b", "text": "<math><mn>600</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b746b"}, {"id": "477733", "text": "<math><mn>570</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b746c"}, {"id": "c70e41", "text": "<math><mn>350</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b746d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b746e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "The current <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> (in <math><mi>A</mi></math> ) flowing through <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistor in the following circuit is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F24bd418d-f63e-485f-9dd8-f49dfa4f5ded.png?alt=media\" style=\"height: 154px; width: 220px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "4ef01a", "text": "<math><mn>0.4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b746f"}, {"id": "ce0ecd", "text": "<math><mn>0.5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7470"}, {"id": "88632d", "text": "<math><mn>0.2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7471"}, {"id": "f1f0fd", "text": "<math><mn>0.25</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7472"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7473", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f36"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eacab"], "question": {"text": "<p>A cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and internal resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is connected with another cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and internal resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> (as shown in the figure). The potential difference across points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> is:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb6c516bc-e0ef-4561-bde0-44c527edc8d6-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 158px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "27e188", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7474"}, {"id": "4f7cfd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7475"}, {"id": "f1db3c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7476"}, {"id": "dd597b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7477"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7478", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b25"], "question": {"text": "The ratio of heat dissipated per second through the resistance $5 \\Omega$ and $10 \\Omega$ in the circuit given below is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7f3mPZgLNMG09vxVmF3VEtLEW48YefqBeBNg5TyA5Zo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "b45602", "text": "$1: 2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7479"}, {"id": "1bf3b2", "text": "$2: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b747a"}, {"id": "583ff0", "text": "$4: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b747b"}, {"id": "fa27fa", "text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b747c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b747d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52aa"], "question": {"text": "A wire of resistance $R$ is bent into a triangular pyramid as shown in figure with each segment having same length. The resistance between points $A$ and $B$ is $R / n$. The value of $n$ is :<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FHsWmDbUUe_Pd9cZYFulcp1g80hj77OA34OGdvg5aHaw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "4eb0d7", "text": "16", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b747e"}, {"id": "7fc3bc", "text": "14", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b747f"}, {"id": "8cdc75", "text": "10", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7480"}, {"id": "e0b6f9", "text": "12", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7481"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7482", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a738"], "question": {"text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> represents the actual number of deflections in a converted galvanometer of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> and shunt resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>. Then the total current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> when its figure of merit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> will be"}, "options": [{"id": "dd4220", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7483"}, {"id": "2609d3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7484"}, {"id": "dde9be", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7485"}, {"id": "c0c19b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>K</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7486"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7487", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566d"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdb66f9ce3f243b5643"], "question": {"text": "The drift velocity of electrons for a conductor connected in an electrical circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math>. The conductor is now replaced by another conductor with same material and same length but double the area of cross-section. The applied voltage remains same. The new drift velocity of electrons will be"}, "options": [{"id": "7b2c7c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7488"}, {"id": "8d7710", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7489"}, {"id": "e70b7e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b748a"}, {"id": "9060b6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b748b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b748c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b19"], "question": {"text": "The resistive network shown below is connected to a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> source of <math><mn>16</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The power consumed by the network is <math><mn>4</mn></math> Watt. The value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb771ee9a-0eb6-4af1-8e8d-64d598e0c4ee-image14.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "de643f", "text": "<math><mn>16</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b748d"}, {"id": "7e072c", "text": "<math><mn>8</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b748e"}, {"id": "7c7673", "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b748f"}, {"id": "b01525", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7490"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7491", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "An electrical power line, having a total resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo></math> delivers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kW</mi></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The efficiency of the transmission line is approximately :"}, "options": [{"id": "0fdd9c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>72</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7492"}, {"id": "85033f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>91</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7493"}, {"id": "c1b382", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>85</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7494"}, {"id": "58068b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>96</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7495"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7496", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c6855"], "question": {"text": "A galvanometer of resistance $100 \\Omega$ when connected in series with $400 \\Omega$ measures a voltage of upto $10 \\mathrm{~V}$. The value of resistance required to convert the galvanometer into ammeter to read upto $10 \\mathrm{~A}$ is $x \\times 10^{-2} \\Omega$. The value of $x$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "18db74", "text": "$2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7497"}, {"id": "cd4bc4", "text": "$800$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7498"}, {"id": "0e7ca4", "text": "$20$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7499"}, {"id": "90a251", "text": "$200$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b749a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b749b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edb"], "question": {"text": "In the experimental set up of metre bridge shown in the figure, the null point is obtaine data distance of $40 \\mathrm{~cm}$ from\n\nA. If a $10 \\Omega$ resistor is connected in series with $\\mathrm{R}_{1},$ the null point shifts by $10 \\mathrm{~cm}$. The resistance that should be connected in parallel with $\\left(\\mathrm{R}_{1}+10\\right) \\Omega$ such that the null point shifts back to its initial position is\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FHsIn7Htb_ptxgoG_scErIUAkGI5hy05ZkJ21SW6Y4Ns.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">"}, "options": [{"id": "40b377", "text": "$20 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b749c"}, {"id": "d65689", "text": "$40 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b749d"}, {"id": "8dfdb3", "text": "$60 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b749e"}, {"id": "b41f9f", "text": "$30 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b749f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b74a0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "The equivalent resistance of the given circuit between the terminals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is :<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2fc36b80-a402-4034-9594-c058eec5d63b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 490px; height: 155px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "b440b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b74a1"}, {"id": "4f8ee3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b74a2"}, {"id": "b08b3f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b74a3"}, {"id": "f40e84", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b74a4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd