69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7535"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7533", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7517", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566d"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c6828"], "question": {"text": "<p>The circuit shown in the figure consists of a charged capacitor of capacity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> and a charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;At time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> when the key is closed, the value of current flowing through the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi>&#937;</mi></math> resistor is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> to the nearest integer is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F892414ba-f6a3-4b94-b212-f6a4189f313e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 163px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "89cbb4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7518"}, {"id": "9db8de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7519"}, {"id": "3acb9c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b751a"}, {"id": "b8aacd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b751b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b751c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given circuit, the current flowing through the resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, while the ammeter reads <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ω</mi></math>.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F278a2f38-0222-451a-84ff-14443e86dfa1.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 183px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "f4d65b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b751d"}, {"id": "be1cfb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b751e"}, {"id": "b490d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b751f"}, {"id": "9ea99f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7520"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7521", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> resistors each of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8486;</mo></math> can be connected in such as to get maximum and minimum equivalent resistance. The ratio of maximum and minimum equivalent resistance will be________."}, "options": [{"id": "64391f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7522"}, {"id": "26e42b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7523"}, {"id": "729763", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7524"}, {"id": "8186c5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7525"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7526", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b25"], "question": {"text": "Two coils require <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> minutes and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math> minutes respectively to produce same amount of heat energy when connected separately to the same source. If they are connected in parallel arrangement to the same source; the time required to produce same amount of heat by the combination of coils, will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>min</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "687354", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7527"}, {"id": "0864c9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7528"}, {"id": "f09ab1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b7529"}, {"id": "5504d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b752a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0d5dcf815cd79b752b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52aa"], "question": {"text": "Four resistances of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=